# __TRAINEE__ — training repo

The context needed to operate this repo. Sessions are **interactive** — you and your
trainer work together; ask questions and iterate freely.

## Startup + first prompt

Per session:

1. **Session start** — you are checked out onto a fresh `session/{date}-{sid8}` branch
   off a clean `main`. You run no git.
2. **First prompt** — paste a `Brief: training/{date}-{curriculum-slug}-{handle}` line
   as the first message; the brief materialises into `.workspace/`. The brief must be
   an **approved** briefs point or the session stops (ask your trainer).
3. **Session end** — the finalise writes your session summary, copies the session log
   into `logs/`, commits your working tree to the session branch, pushes, and opens a
   **PR to `main`**. Your next session reviews + merges that PR, then continues.

## Where work goes

Everything lands under `__TRAINEE__/`: `sourceDocs/` (external material — add it here
before use), `inputDocs/` (your documents), `outputDocs/` (assistant-produced
documents), `sessions/` (per-session notes). Never write at the repo root. Session
context comes **only** from this repo plus the `.workspace/` task repos the brief
materialises (context containment) — copy anything external into `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/`
first.

## Agent

- **Name:** __TRAINEE__
- **Team:** training
- **Role:** trainee (interactive sessions)
- **Operator:** Trainee

## First-run setup

This repo needs one-time workstation setup before a brief will load — see
`docs/workstation-setup.md` (trainer-assisted) and `docs/dependency-analysis.md` (the
full dependency list). Run `python3 .claude/hooks/trainee-preflight.py` to check what is
still missing. Until setup is complete the hooks fail **soft**: one "not configured yet
— see the setup guide" pointer, never a wall of errors, and orientation is never
blocked.

## Hook set

| Event | Script | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| SessionStart | `session-start.sh` | Telemetry + unfinalised-session guard |
| SessionStart | `trainee-session-branch.py` | Branch onto `session/{date}-{sid8}` off main |
| UserPromptSubmit | `first-prompt-brief.py` | Parse the `Brief:` id + materialise `.workspace/` |
| PreToolUse | `pre-tool-use.sh` | Telemetry + report out-of-repo reads (context containment) |
| PostToolUse | `post-tool-use.sh` | Tool-result telemetry |
| Stop | `stop.sh` | Session tasking checkpoint |
| SessionEnd | `session-end-finalise.py` | Summary → copy session log into `logs/` → commit + push + PR to main |

## Constraints

- All work lands under `__TRAINEE__/` — never at the repo root.
- You run no git — the hooks own branching, commit, and the session PR.
- `context/` and `.workspace/` are ephemeral — never commit them.
- Secrets via the workstation env block / secrets MCP only — never hardcode or log a
  secret; if a secret appears in context, stop and tell your trainer.
